 Acme Logistics.
 ```
 
+**Asking through a tool.** While a sheet is attached the model is also offered
+`ask_user_question`, with one string argument, `question`. The same judge reads the
+question against the sheet, in the same side call, and its tokens count the same way.
+
+- On a hit the tool result is the selected entries, verbatim, and the run goes on. The
+  `tool_result` event carries `source: "oracle"` and the selected ids as `keys`, and the
+  trailer's `oracle_turns` counts it.
+- With no entry to give, the result is `The user has no answer to that question. Proceed
+  on your own judgement.` and the run goes on. This is not `oracle_miss`: the model
+  called a tool and is still working, so there is no halt to label. The event carries
+  `source: "oracle"` and no ids.
+- A hit spends one of `budget oracle_turns`, shared with end-of-turn resolutions. A
+  question that has an answer after the budget is spent gets `The user is no longer
+  answering questions in this run.` and the run ends `oracle_budget`.
+
+A program with no `oracle` never offers the tool: a question nobody can answer would be
+a trap. On Mock, `MOCK:tool=ask_user_question <text>` sends `<text>` as the question,
+and a `MOCK:oracle=` rider in it scripts the verdict.
+
 **Authoring a sheet.** Key entries by topic, not by question; models phrase one question
 ten ways. Write each body as the full answer a real user would give, with enough detail
